-- statement:
--   The rational value is returned in scalar cell 6, with its canonical sign in cell 7 (negative sign), cells 10 through 10+k−1
--   (numerator), and the next k cells (denominator). Padding consists of high zero digits.
--   No bit of an input scalar is a machine operation.
--
--   This lemma is part of OpenAI's machine-checked proof that rational linear programs can be solved by a strongly polynomial algorithm on a real-number RAM (Smale's ninth problem). It is used in the proof of `OAI.Optimization.LinearProgramming.Compression.publishWireComponents_spec`.
